<title>USA: Bargains among temporary staffing stocks - NYT.</title>
<headline>Bargains among temporary staffing stocks - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stocks of temporary-staffing companies have declined lately but many analysts believe much of the slump was unwarranted, the New York Times said on Sunday.</p>
<p>For some companies, like Olsten Corp, the decline made some sense since about half of the company's revenues came from health care, a field under public and cost pressure, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>But because many staffing companies offered a blend of services, they were not so vulnerable to cyclical dangers, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The stocks were also cheap, Judith Scott, a research analyst at Baird, was quoted as saying. Her picks included Accustaff and Interim Services Inc.</p>
</text>
